00:14:40,730 --> 00:14:43,810
Oh... uh, okay.

259
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:51,310
Miyamura...

260
00:14:51,310 --> 00:14:55,900
I thought you were the kind of guy
who could never stand up for himself.

261
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:57,940
I thought you were some loser.

262
00:14:57,940 --> 00:15:02,060
But guess it's easy for you to be
confident around your girlfriend, huh?

263
00:15:02,060 --> 00:15:03,100
Yeah, super easy.

264
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:07,770
Whoa, why are your eyes all red?!
Were you rubbing them or something?!

265
00:15:12,940 --> 00:15:16,730
Miyamura! Go away, there's not enough room!

266
00:15:16,730 --> 00:15:17,900
Go where?

267
00:15:17,900 --> 00:15:21,350
Outside, jeez! Where are we, anyway?!

268
00:15:21,350 --> 00:15:22,650
Outside.

269
00:15:22,650 --> 00:15:23,520
Huh?

270
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:27,230
This is outside. The only free space there is.

271
00:15:27,230 --> 00:15:31,560
What the hell?! This locker
or whatever isn't "outside" at all!

272
00:15:31,560 --> 00:15:35,270
This is what it's like "outside."

273
00:15:35,270 --> 00:15:39,600
You've always been on the "inside,"
so you don't know how it feels.

274
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:43,190
Inside, outside, what the hell are you on about?

275
00:15:43,190 --> 00:15:45,560
You're the one who brought it up.

276
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:51,020
I think this is the first time
we've ever talked like this.

277
00:15:51,020 --> 00:15:52,900
Do you not like tight spaces?

278
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:54,400
I hate them.

279
00:15:54,400 --> 00:15:57,480
Huh. So do I.

280
00:15:57,480 --> 00:15:59,020
